  "column_notes": {
    "species_taxid": "NCBI species-rank taxid. The join key. Never join on a name: NCBI labels the same taxon with more than one name.",
    "species_name": "The name of species_taxid in the NCBI taxonomy, not the name the submitter deposited.",
    "scientific_name": "The name the submitter deposited. May be a synonym, a strain-level name, or a rank above species.",
    "exclusion": "'' or mutant, evolution, cross, not_wgs. A LABEL from the study and sample titles. Nothing is deleted. Filter it yourself.",
    "est_depth_x": "base_count divided by the NCBI reference assembly size for the species. An estimate from metadata, not a measurement on reads. Blank when no reference size resolved.",
    "ncbi_status": "in_ncbi, ena_only, or not_checked. Only the 113 species with 100 or more isolates were reconciled against NCBI.",
    "fastq_ftp": "';'-joined ENA FTP paths, no scheme. Prepend https://.",
    "fastq_aspera": "';'-joined Aspera paths for the ENA fasp endpoint.",
    "country": "Exactly as the submitter wrote it. Free text. Use country_iso to group.",
    "country_iso": "ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 (XK for Kosovo). Blank unless country_status is ok. Parsed from country by popseq/normalise.py (issue #23).",
    "country_status": "ok, absent (field empty), missing (an explicit INSDC missing term such as 'not collected'), region (ocean, continent), historical (e.g. Yugoslavia), conflicting (multi-sample run whose samples disagree), unresolved (add it to catalog/vocab/country_aliases.csv).",
    "host": "Raw host from the BioSample: first non-empty of host, host_plant, specific hosts, host_common_name.",
    "host_taxid": "NCBI taxid of host. Blank unless host_status is ok or same_as_organism. Resolved via catalog/vocab/host_taxa.csv.gz.",
    "host_status": "ok, absent, missing, not_a_host (a lab or environment term such as 'soil' or 'culture'), same_as_organism (the host field names the sequenced organism itself), ambiguous, conflicting, unresolved.",
    "library_layout": "PAIRED or SINGLE as the submitter labelled it. Metadata only: wrong for 2,274 catalog runs. Use ena_layout.",
    "ena_layout": "PAIRED when ENA serves _1 and _2 files, SINGLE when it serves one file, blank when none. Decides pairing and the --layout filter (spec 001). NCBI may still hold a PAIRED run unpaired; the fetcher checks that (spec 002).",
    "read_count": "Read pairs for SRR/DRR runs but reads for most ERR runs. Not a verification target (spec 002).",
    "label_species": "Species named by a curated authority (catalog/labels/sources.csv), not by the submitter. ';'-joined when the authority cannot choose between species (label_status tie). Blank when it makes no call.",
    "label_complex": "The species complex all names in label_species share, from the authority. Blank when they differ or when there is no label.",
    "label_status": "confident (one species), tie (several, ';'-joined) or no_call.",
    "label_agreement": "same, tie_includes_ncbi, differs, ncbi_unnamed (the NCBI name is sp./cf. or blank) or no_call, against ncbi_species.",
    "ncbi_species": "The NCBI taxonomy name of the assembly's species_taxid, or the deposited organism name when the taxid is not in the taxonomy map.",
    "curated_species": "A curator's species for this assembly. Ours, entered by hand, never overwritten by an import. When set it wins over label_species.",
    "sample_accession": "BioSample. In the raw ENA export this field is sometimes ';'-joined for multi-sample runs (issue #3)."
  },
  "caveats": [
    "Every count is a floor. ENA holds runs with an empty tax_id that no taxonomy query reaches, so the true per-species totals are higher (issue #2).",
    "A run count is not a strain count and an isolate count is not an independent-sample count. 52 of the 113 largest species take half or more of their isolates from one study. Read catalog/summary/clonality.csv.gz before treating a species as a population.",
    "est_depth_x comes from metadata, not from the reads.",
    "Only 113 species were reconciled against NCBI. For every other species ncbi_status is not_checked, which is not the same as absent.",
    "Nothing here has been downloaded or verified. These are archive records.",
    "Scope: the run table holds only ENA runs with library_strategy=WGS and library_source=GENOMIC, on instrument_platform ILLUMINA (snapshot 2026-11-06) or BGISEQ/DNBSEQ (supplement 2026-11-09; scripts/popseq_snapshot.py). A --strategy filter for anything else returns nothing because those runs were never harvested, not because none exist (issue #24). The --platform filter defaults to ILLUMINA; pass BGISEQ, DNBSEQ or '' to see the others."
  ]
}
